# smoke-scale env: widerpbw + bit-pair interaction terms (scale=1.0).
#
# Aggressive variant of .env_smoke_pair_0p5 — pair coefficients drawn from
# U(0, 1.0) instead of U(0, 0.5). Pair-signal variance dominates linear by
# roughly an order of magnitude at this scale; templates should see the
# strongest possible bit-pair contribution. Run in parallel with the 0.5
# config to bracket the response curve.
#
# Inherits from .env_smoke_byte_pbw_widerpbw with two changes:
#   SIM_PAIR_BYTE_SCALE=1.0  (NEW: enable bit-pair terms, aggressive scale)
#   SIM_HD_RATIO=0.0         (HD off)
#
# Pairs with the sim-bit-pair-leakage branch's KeccakSim_BI_TA.py +
# run_full_pipeline.sh.

